  "body": "Stacked on #3092 for the default-machine diagnostic. Review [the template changes above that head](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/d0fe169a159a14dc5a5973a6c9af332ad70a6cc1...f2cc7ac5010e305b0ca73bbb8cf25938137f96c4).\n\n## Change\n\nAdd the AGIECUT Classic 2S wire EDM machine template to the desktop and embedded machine libraries. Mounting the template preserves the selected post.\n\nThe template states the X/Y rapid speed of 900 mm/min, the Z/U/V rapid speed of 600 mm/min and U/V travel of ±70 mm. It lists the four standard wire sizes from 0.20 to 0.33 mm. The X/Y/Z stroke lengths appear in the description. The operator supplies the installed datum, guide planes and cutting conditions. The handbook qualifies its maximum taper angle by guide type and work height.\n\nThe native job post is separate work in #2945. This change does not select an Agie dialect.\n\n## Source\n\n[AGIE, AGIECUT Classic technical handbook, edition 06.2002 C2.1](https://static.gindumac.com/products/9ccc9b7e-b589-49db-9843-eff1da09434c/documents/ES-EDM-AGI-2002-00001.pdf). Section 1.1 on printed page 4 identifies the model group, travels and speeds. Section 5.2 on printed page 44 lists the wire sizes.\n\n## Verification\n\nIndependent checks used head 08601a2bc. All 68 tests in machine, machine_library, mcp_wire_contour and posting passed. Clippy passed on all camcraft-app targets with warnings denied.\n\nThe pinning tests are:\n- agiecut_classic_2s_exposes_the_sourced_axes_and_wire_sizes\n- agiecut_template_refuses_a_wire_job_without_an_installed_condition\n- every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration\n\nThe normal command script selected the exact library name and mounted AGIECUT CLASSIC 2S. An attempted wire job with C110 failed with a missing-condition diagnostic. It created no NC file. Physical travel and cutting were not tested.\n\nOn the refreshed head f2cc7ac50, the full quick gate passed all 256 steps in 36.0 minutes. The verifier rebuilt it in its own target directory on macOS arm64. The axis-direction, default-machine and process-folder suites passed all 23 targeted tests. The complete reached heavy gate passed all 196 steps in 58.4 minutes. Both debug and release executables resolved the template from this checkout. Verification used `cargo xtask gate quick --base 1d81b609c` and `cargo xtask gate heavy --base 1d81b609c`.\n\nThe former head had two inherited failures: its per-operation refusal named only the setup, and its optimized bore fixture used different platform counts. The refreshed head includes the upstream Apple silicon fixture and the default-machine correction in #3092.\n\nThe standalone Generic ISO wire post also reported missing machine codes on a committed contour stream. The machine template supplies machine data. The operator still needs a suitable post and an installed cutting condition.\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: The machine library includes an AGIECUT Classic 2S wire EDM template with the manufacturer's stated axes, rapid speeds and standard wire sizes.\n\nFixes #2946\n\n\n",
